\begin_layout Standard
This report provides analysis and presentation of measured data for the
 storage system
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
/$-SiteId 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
SiteDescription 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The storage unit is located at
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It enables installation and operation of an enlarged PV-Generator with 2.5
 times higher peak power by means of buffering PV generation, ensuring the
 line power to stay within the limits allowed.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\noindent
The report is conforming with the EC Guidelines for unified monitoring and
 performance assessement of storage-units in the grid structure.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\noindent
Thus, it reveals energy balancing in a subgrid, characterized by both energy
 surplus and autonomy ratio.
 Further it quantifies and details contribution of the storage unit to grid
 control and balancing, and thus relief of the utility interface, resp.
 power line.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\noindent
In the form of directed power-flows, monitoring data is suitable for spatial
 aggregation with results from other storage units in a common grid area.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\noindent
Further to reporting for storage and distribution system operators, guideline
 conformant data and monitoring evaluation qualify for sharing performance
 experience, e.g.
 in the JRC's storage observatory.
\end_layout

